  "text": "9:41¢ ull ¥ @\n| r\n1.2. what is the modern era?\n1.2 what is the modern era?\nweek 1: intro\ntranscript notes summary attachments\n\n0:05 now we come to another question. what is the modern\nera? where do we start?\n\n0:13 and why do we start where we start? it is very common\nand customary in the writing of middle eastern history\nto start the modern era in 1798. why 1798?\n\n0:28 because in 1798 napoleon invaded egypt, and ushered\nin through his invasion, a long period of rapid and\nradical change. that sounds reasonable. but it is\nproblematic.\n\n0:47 because in this determination of the napoleonic\ninvasion as the beginning of the modern era, there is a\nhidden assumption. that hidden assumption is, that\nthe modern era in the middle east was created only and\nsolely through european influence and european\nsupremacy on an area which is in decline, stagnant and\nmoving nowhere. so there is now a historiographical\ndebate about whether it was ever really correct to begin\nthe modern era with the napoleonic invasion of egypt.\nthe ltalian historiassandwekilecanher benedgetta-lrace\n\n< previous =+ save a note next\n",
